      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--tokenizer-worker-num` > 1, a tokenizer worker drops every INFO line except those from `sglang.srt.entrypoints.http_server`. Only warnings get through, so anything the tokenizer manager, a multimodal processor or an external plugin logs at INFO from a worker is lost.\n\nRoot cause:\n- The workers are ASGI worker processes: uvicorn's, started by `uvicorn.run(..., workers=N)`, or Granian's with `--enable-http2`.\n- They keep the server's logging config. For uvicorn that is `LOGGING_CONFIG`, to which `launch_server` adds only `sglang.srt.entrypoints.http_server` at INFO. That is why a worker still prints `Start multi-tokenizer worker process`.\n- `init_multi_tokenizer` never calls `configure_logger`; the scheduler, detokenizer and DP controller each do.\n- So the worker's root logger stays at Python's default WARNING.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `init_multi_tokenizer` calls `configure_logger(server_args, prefix=\" TokenizerWorker-<pid>\")` right after it reads the server args, before it builds the tokenizer manager.\n  - The prefix tells the N workers' lines apart.\n  - `basicConfig(force=True)` replaces only the root logger's handlers. uvicorn's own loggers (own handlers, `propagate: False`) and the `http_server` logger keep theirs, so nothing is logged twice.\n- `test/registered/tokenizer/test_multi_tokenizer.py`:\n  - `TestMultiTokenizer` now captures the server's output. It is still echoed to stdout.\n  - It gains `test_every_tokenizer_worker_logs_at_info`, which asserts that INFO lines arrive under 8 distinct `TokenizerWorker-<pid>` prefixes. It polls for up to 30 s, since the server answers as soon as one worker is up.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: logging only.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: logging only.\n\n## Tests\n\n| test | `main` (`59eb71a831`) | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| `TestMultiTokenizer.test_every_tokenizer_worker_logs_at_info` (Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, 8 workers, one L20) | fails: `0 != 8` | passes |\n\nWith 2 workers on the small test model, each worker now logs, for example, `Using default chat sampling params from model generation config` under its own prefix. On `main` none of these lines appear.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (Not needed.)\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (Not applicable.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01RbA69Qr9sS5ksRCQCwTKyN\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37929750820](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37929750820)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37929750449](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37929750449)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37929750713](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37929750713)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
